==English==

===Alternative spellings===
* [[any more]] (''UK'', ''Australia'', ''New Zealand'')

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-anymore.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|ɔː(r)}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}
# At the [[present]] [[time]]; [[any longer]].
#: ''They don't make repairable radios '''anymore'''.''
# Starting from the [[present]] [[time]]; [[from now on]].
#: ''I won't be naughty '''anymore'''.''

===Usage notes===
* Normally used in a negative phrase.
*Regional note: In standard American English {{term||anymore}} is often found in negative sentences: {{term||They don't live here anymore}}. But {{term||anymore}} is widely used in regional American English[[Category:American English]] in positive sentences with the meaning "nowadays": {{term||We use a gas stove anymore}} (Oklahoma informant in [[DARE]]). Its use is centered in the South Midland and Midwestern states, as well as in the Western states that received settlers from those areas. The earliest recorded examples are from Northern Ireland, where the positive use of anymore still occurs.

